<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Psusennes II</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">10th century BCE</span> · Also known as Pasebakhaenniut II</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Psusennes II was the last king of the Twenty-first Dynasty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>, reigning in the mid-10th century BCE. He may also have held the office of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/high-priest-of-amun">High Priest of Amun</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thebes">Thebes</a>, uniting the northern kingship and the Theban priesthood. On his death the throne passed peacefully to his relative by marriage, the Libyan chief <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shoshenq-i">Shoshenq I</a>, founder of the Twenty-second Dynasty.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/psusennes-ii.jpg" alt="Psusennes II" width="320" height="480" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Georges Legrain (1865-1917) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Statue_CG42192_legrain.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
